  "notes": "Describes things being scattered or strewn about in a disorderly way. Combines {散|さん} (scatter) and {乱|らん} (disorder), emphasizing the messy, chaotic nature of the scattering.\n\nUSAGE:\n- Most commonly used with {散乱|さんらん}している (state of being scattered)\n- Often describes the aftermath of storms, accidents, or general untidiness\n- In physics, {散乱|さんらん} also refers to the scattering of light or particles\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- ゴミが{散乱|さんらん}する: garbage is strewn about\n- {書類|しょるい}が{散乱|さんらん}する: documents are scattered\n- {破片|はへん}が{散乱|さんらん}する: fragments are scattered\n- {光|ひかり}の{散乱|さんらん}: scattering of light (physics)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {散|ち}らかる: to be messy, cluttered — more casual and everyday\n- {散|ち}らばる: to be scattered — neutral, without the disorder nuance\n- {乱雑|らんざつ}: messy, disorderly — describes the state rather than the act of scattering",
